<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87754" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προκατ-έχω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hold</i> or <i>gain possession of beforehand,
				preoccupy,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν πόλιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.105
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἄκρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					5.4.59
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν διάπλουν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					1.61.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς παρόδους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Nic.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ τὸ προκατεσχῆσθαι φρουρᾷ [τὴν
					ἄκραν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					8.31.1
				</span></i>
			: simply, <i>occupy,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃν προκατεῖχε τόπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>Tact.</u>
					25.7
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>hold down before oneself,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προκατέσχετο χερσὶ καλύπτρην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Cer.</u>
					197
				</span></i>
			: metaph. in 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be prejudiced,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. εὐνοίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					8.31.3
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				27.4.9
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				9.31.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαβολαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phalar.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					56
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be predetermined,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφ᾽ ἑτέρας αἰτίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diogenian.Epicur.
					3.60
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr., <i>to
				be superior,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς ἡλικίαις καὶ ταῖς δόξαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					27.15.7
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγέλης</span>
			<i>to be leaders of</i> the herd, of bulls, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				6.200d
			</span></i>.</div>
